# Content publishing plan (canonical)

Follow this schedule and these conventions unless the user explicitly changes them.

## Rhythm (locked)

- **2 posts per week**
- **Blog + LinkedIn on the same evening** (never split across days)
- **Publish days: Tuesday and Thursday only** — no Friday (low evening engagement)
- **Window:** ~7:30–9:30 PM IST (deploy/verify blog earlier; LinkedIn after Post Inspector)
- **Buffer:** Finish the next post before the prior publish day; Tue/Thu are ship-only
- **Same-evening checklist:** deploy → verify live URL → LinkedIn Post Inspector → post caption → reply to comments ~1h

## If a slot slips

| Missed | Move to |
|--------|---------|
| Tuesday | Following Thursday (not Friday) |
| Thursday | Following Tuesday |
| Whole week | Drop the lightest post; never skip series anchors below |

**Anchors (do not drop):** Kafka foundation/hands-on, Trees-style algorithm launches, System Design #1 (URL shortener template).

## Three series

| Series | Shape | ~Per month |
|--------|--------|------------|
| **Algorithms** | Interactive pattern guides (animations, practice ladder) | 2 |
| **Kafka** | Progressive arc — why → vocab → hands-on → groups → compare → ops | 2 |
| **System Design** | **One problem per post** — not topic dumps | 2 |

Homepage **Start here** stays **Kafka** until System Design has **3+** published posts. Then reconsider.

### Cross-links

- SD Notification / feed / chat → Kafka series (why, vocab, produce/consume, groups)
- Algorithms heaps/trees ↔ SD when priority queues or hierarchies appear
- Plain examples: order → stock → email → shipping (see `example-domain` rule). No invented brands.

## Writing voice (all series)

- Problem-first opening; interactive early when it teaches
- One clear insight per section — avoid repeating the same takeaway 3–4 times (“Remember this…” + sticky × N + take-home dump)
- **Do not** label sections “for beginners” / “for experienced readers” — weave depth into the main flow
- LinkedIn: problem hook, ~3 bullets, one deep link, one question — no “Post N of series” framing unless useful

### System Design post template

1. Problem statement (who, scale hint, constraints)
2. Clarify (interactive questions)
3. Capacity / back-of-envelope (interactive if useful)
4. API + data model
5. Step-up architecture (add pieces only when a bottleneck appears)
6. Failures / scale
7. Tradeoffs
8. Interview takeaways (short)

Interactives to prefer: clarify quiz, capacity slider, architecture steps, bottleneck picker, tradeoff cards.

